{
  "version": "1.0",
  "kernel": "st-lang",
  "kernelVersion": "4.14",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Introducción a Lógica Clásica",
    "author": "Agora Education",
    "profile": "classical.propositional",
    "createdAt": "2026-05-18T00:00:00.000Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-05-18T00:00:00.000Z"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell-intro-md",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Introducción a Lógica Propositional Clásica\n\nEn esta sesión exploraremos las tautologías fundamentales.\nComenzamos con el teorema de identidad: $p \\to p$."
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-identity",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "check valid (P -> P)",
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-modus-md",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Modus Ponens\n\nSi tenemos $P \\to Q$ y $P$, podemos derivar $Q$.\n\n$$\\frac{P \\to Q \\quad P}{Q} MP$$"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-modus-ponens",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "axiom a1 : P -> Q\naxiom a2 : P\nderive Q from a1, a2",
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-de-morgan-md",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Leyes de De Morgan\n\nLas leyes de De Morgan son fundamentales:\n- $\\lnot(P \\land Q) \\equiv \\lnot P \\lor \\lnot Q$\n- $\\lnot(P \\lor Q) \\equiv \\lnot P \\land \\lnot Q$"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell-de-morgan",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "check valid (not (P and Q)) <-> ((not P) or (not Q))",
      "outputs": []
    }
  ]
}
